# The homepage, from the copy frontend/prerender.js stamps at /prerendered/home
# (canonical, title, JSON-LD and a body in the raw HTML). dist/index.html can't
# carry those itself: Pages also serves it for every URL without a file of its
# own, so it would claim to be the homepage on all of them. A rewrite (200),
# not a redirect: the URL stays /. Should the copy ever be missing, Pages
# answers with that same fallback shell, which is what / served before.
/  /prerendered/home  200

# /about is a common guess for the author page, which lives at /nick-twort
